  "providerImslp": "IMSLP privacy policy",
  "termsIntro": "These terms describe use of the CantaVue website and current app. Contact the CantaVue project at info@cantavue.com. Installation and use also follow the distribution platform's applicable agreements; this page does not replace Apple's standard license agreement.",
  "terms1Title": "Version and feature scope",
  "terms1Body": "Available features depend on your installed version, supported system and enabled services. Website scenario images are labeled illustrations, not hardware certification, customer endorsements or guarantees of unreleased features. TestFlight eligibility and builds depend on a valid invitation and platform status; a beta invitation does not mean an official App Store version has launched.",
  "terms2Title": "Your scores and content rights",
  "terms2Body": "You retain rights you hold in scores, annotations, recordings and other content. Import, record, download or share only material you have permission to use, including any required permission for other people’s recordings or personal information. Using the app grants no rights to third-party scores; public availability does not establish permission in every region. Do not use the service to infringe rights, distribute unlawful content or interfere with others.",
  "terms3Title": "Saving, backups and performances",
  "terms3Body": "Keep original scores and independent backups of important annotations, practice and teaching data. Local saving, file export, server confirmation and another device's receipt are different states. Check recipients and included information before sharing; switching teaching workspaces does not isolate identities on shared devices. Test performance workflows, accessories and reminders beforehand, and keep an appropriate reading alternative. Unexpected errors may cause interruptions or data loss.",
  "terms4Title": "Third-party services and devices",
  "terms4Body": "IMSLP, system file providers, your WebDAV or compatible sync server, configured cloud services and TestFlight are operated by their respective providers. Their terms, content rights and availability apply. Connecting does not mean automatic sync; forgetting a local account does not revoke all provider access or delete remote files. Camera, stylus, MIDI, pedal and notification features depend on the system, permissions and hardware. Illustrations do not guarantee every model's compatibility.",
  "terms5Title": "Charges, licenses and feedback",
  "terms5Body": "The current version has no in-app purchase flow. Future pricing or paid features will be described separately; submitting feedback does not start a subscription. CantaVue-owned app, website and brand materials are protected by applicable rights; third-party and open-source materials retain their licenses. We may use voluntary suggestions to improve the product without taking ownership of private scores, recordings or attachments.",
  "terms6Title": "Responsibility, statutory rights and changes",
  "terms6Body": "We provide the app according to its current features without guaranteeing error-free operation on every device or in every situation. Any liability limitation applies only where permitted by law and does not exclude non-excludable liability or consumer rights. Material changes will update this page's date and be notified where required. Contact info@cantavue.com with questions.",
  "supportIntro": "Email info@cantavue.com for help, suggestions or privacy requests. Your own mail app sends the message; this page does not automatically upload information.",
  "supportEmailAction": "Email feedback",
  "support1Title": "Help us reproduce the issue",
  "support1Body": "Include your device model, OS version, app version and build number, steps, expected result and actual result. Redacted screenshots can help. Do not send passwords, session links, private scores or student information. TestFlight testers can also use the feedback option in TestFlight.",
  "support2Title": "Get started",
  "support2Body": "In the library choose New score, open a built-in staff-paper template, enter a title and create it to try reading, annotations, saving and reopening without an account or private file. You can also choose Import score → Open files for a PDF you are authorized to use. Teaching offers local student and schedule workspaces; recipients still need to import exported files.",
  "support3Title": "Save and recover",
  "support3Body": "Wait for saving to finish, return to the library and reopen the score to confirm your annotations. Export important scores and complete backups before updating. Try recovery with test data first. If something goes wrong, preserve original files and backups instead of repeatedly overwriting them.",
  "support4Title": "Permissions and beta access",
  "support4Body": "Photography, practice recordings, teaching voice feedback, live tuning, nearby sessions, and local practice or lesson reminders request permission only when you choose the feature. Manage access in system settings and review notification previews and quiet hours. Local reminders do not remotely notify students. Join the iOS and iPadOS beta through this website's TestFlight invitation; available builds and installation eligibility are shown in TestFlight.",
  "feedbackEmail": "info@cantavue.com"
}
